{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1028","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1028","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1028\",\"parent_revision\":\"e5151dd63dd1c5e9f11ed08a9517c8617f45523f\",\"root_revision\":\"999cd1cb7849887e7af0ba41bf1887cc7f9bad9dd92916528f8b3f5bc4576f32\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nplugin-creator should be a superset of Anthropic's plugin-dev plugin. A rebase analysis (2026-03-24) identified 3 gaps where plugin-dev has content that plugin-creator does not cover.\\n\\nGap 1 \u2014 command-development skill (largest). plugin-dev has a full skill at plugins/plugin-dev/skills/command-development/ covering the legacy commands/ format with distinct frontmatter fields (disable-model-invocation, argument-hint spec), argument syntax ($IF(), ${1:-default} defaults), state management via .local.md files, workflow locking, rollback patterns, and a 7-level testing hierarchy. plugin-creator has no equivalent.\\n\\nGap 2 \u2014 hook/mcp/agent/settings skill depth. plugin-dev has skills for hook-development, mcp-integration, agent-development, and plugin-settings. plugin-creator covers these topics but reference-file depth has not been compared. An interactive-commands.md reference in plugin-dev (AskUserQuestion and user-interaction patterns) was not read during the analysis.\\n\\nGap 3 \u2014 component decision framework. plugin-dev has \\\"when to use which component\\\" guidance for choosing between skills, commands, agents, hooks, and MCP servers. plugin-creator does not have an explicit decision framework for this.\\n\\nSource material for investigation \u2014 Anthropic plugin-dev at ../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/ and rebase analysis report at .claude/reports/plugin-dev-rebase-analysis.md\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: plugin-creator superset gaps vs Anthropic plugin-dev\\nGoal: Make plugin-creator a superset of Anthropic's plugin-dev by closing 3 identified content gaps (command-development skill, hook/mcp/agent/settings depth, component decision framework).\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 all conditions resolved.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Source material at ../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/ | AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst confirmed 7 files in command-development/ skill directory\\n2. Rebase analysis report at .claude/reports/plugin-dev-rebase-analysis.md | AVAILABLE | Citation: groomer read report successfully\\n3. Gap 1 \u2014 command-development content readable from plugin-dev | AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst confirmed 7 source files; feature-researcher confirmed 11 files total\\n4. Gap 2 \u2014 hook/mcp/agent/settings depth comparison | DERIVABLE | Resolved via T1 prerequisite research task in P1028\\n5. Gap 3 \u2014 component decision framework in plugin-dev | AVAILABLE | Citation: source identified as plugin-dev/skills/plugin-structure/references/component-patterns.md\\n6. plugin-creator current skill structure | AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst mapped 14 affected systems\\n7. Target placement for new content | AVAILABLE | Citation: architect spec defines exact file paths for all 9 deliverables\\n8. Editorial stance on legacy commands framing | RESOLVED | User decision (2026-03-24): Option A \u2014 preserve legacy framing note from plugin-dev (\\\"commands/ is a legacy format\\\") at top of new command-development skill. No change to skill-creator/references/claude-code-skills-official.md needed.\\n\\nPlan: P1028-plugin-creator-superset-gaps-vs-anthropic-plugin-dev.yaml (9 tasks, 3 priority waves)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n\\n**Rationale**: Plugin-creator lacks decision-framework guidance that exists in plugin-dev. Specifically:\\n1. No component decision framework (when to use skill vs command vs agent vs hook vs MCP server)\\n2. Missing command-development skill coverage\\n3. Incomplete reference depth for hook/MCP/agent/settings compared to plugin-dev\\n\\nWithout this guidance, plugin developers make suboptimal component choices (e.g., implementing workflows as commands when skills would be cleaner, or vice versa). The three identified gaps represent systematic holes in the decision-support content, not defects in existing functionality.\\n\\n**Impact**: Affects quality and consistency of plugin implementations within this repository and marketplace submissions.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/SKILL.md` \u2014 NEW FILE to create: primary skill entry point for the command-development gap (Gap 1). Does not exist yet; creation is the core deliverable.\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/references/frontmatter-reference.md` \u2014 NEW FILE: command-specific frontmatter (`disable-model-invocation`, `allowed-tools` with Bash filter syntax, `argument-hint` format). Sourced from plugin-dev equivalent.\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/references/advanced-workflows.md` \u2014 NEW FILE: state management, locking, checkpoint/recovery, command composition. Sourced from plugin-dev equivalent.\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/references/interactive-commands.md` \u2014 NEW FILE: AskUserQuestion and user-interaction patterns for commands. Sourced from plugin-dev equivalent.\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-plugins-reference-2026/SKILL.md` \u2014 CONTENT UPDATE: add component decision framework section (Gap 3) covering \\\"when to use skill vs command vs agent vs hook vs MCP\\\". Currently reference documentation only; needs decision guidance added.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-creator/SKILL.md` \u2014 will need to reference new `command-development` skill once created, so users are routed to it for command creation workflows.\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md` \u2014 lifecycle skill that orchestrates creation phases; may need to route command creation tasks to the new command-development skill.\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-skills-overview-2026/SKILL.md` \u2014 currently notes `commands/` as legacy format; needs cross-reference to new command-development skill once it exists.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/claude-code-skills-official.md` \u2014 currently contains a note that `commands/` is a legacy format and skills are preferred. The new command-development skill should co-exist with this note; the reference should be updated to point to the new skill rather than leaving command development undocumented.\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/agent-plugin-ecosystem.md` \u2014 documents cross-vendor portability; command frontmatter fields (`allowed-tools`, `disable-model-invocation`) are relevant to portability. Verify no stale claims once command-development skill is authored.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/claude-code-skills-official.md` \u2014 section on commands as legacy format will become inaccurate if new command-development skill signals commands are still viable (not purely legacy). Needs reconciliation.\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-plugins-reference-2026/SKILL.md` \u2014 component reference section will become stale if decision framework content is added without updating the reference index or ToC.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 auto-bumped by pre-commit hook on any commit that adds files under `plugins/plugin-creator/`; no manual change needed. New skill directory will be auto-discovered (skills are in default location `skills/` \u2014 no explicit `skills` key in plugin.json needed).\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/.claude-plugin/validator.json` \u2014 validator schema for plugin-creator; verify new skill passes `uvx skilllint@latest check` after creation. No config change needed unless new reference file patterns violate schema.\\n- `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` \u2014 version auto-bumped by pre-commit hook; no manual change needed.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-creator/SKILL.md` \u2014 orchestration skill that routes creation requests; will need to route \\\"create a command\\\" requests to `plugin-creator:command-development` once the skill exists.\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/audit-skill-completeness/SKILL.md` \u2014 completeness auditor; scope may expand to include command-development completeness checks. Verify whether audit criteria need updating.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n| Path | Role | Connection |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/` | Producer (new) | Gap 1 deliverable \u2014 does not exist, must be created |\\n| `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/references/frontmatter-reference.md` | Producer (new) | Gap 1 reference content \u2014 command-specific frontmatter fields |\\n| `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/references/advanced-workflows.md` | Producer (new) | Gap 1 reference content \u2014 state management, locking, rollback |\\n| `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/references/interactive-commands.md` | Producer (new) | Gap 2 from rebase analysis \u2014 AskUserQuestion patterns |\\n| `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-plugins-reference-2026/SKILL.md` | Producer (update) | Gap 3 \u2014 decision framework (skill vs command vs agent vs hook vs MCP) |\\n| `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-creator/SKILL.md` | Consumer | Orchestration router \u2014 needs pointer to new command-development skill |\\n| `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md` | Consumer | Lifecycle orchestrator \u2014 may need routing update for command creation |\\n| `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-skills-overview-2026/SKILL.md` | Consumer | Cross-reference \u2014 notes commands as legacy; needs update |\\n| `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/claude-code-skills-official.md` | Other reference | Legacy commands note \u2014 needs reconciliation with new skill's framing |\\n| `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/agent-plugin-ecosystem.md` | Other reference | Portability docs \u2014 verify command frontmatter claims remain accurate |\\n| `plugins/plugin-creator/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` | Configuration | Auto-bumped on commit; auto-discovers new skill directory |\\n| `plugins/plugin-creator/.claude-plugin/validator.json` | Configuration | Validate new skill passes skilllint after creation |\\n| `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` | Configuration | Auto-bumped on commit |\\n| `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/audit-skill-completeness/SKILL.md` | Agent instruction | Completeness auditor \u2014 may need scope expansion |\\n\\n**Source of truth for gap content:**\\n- `../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/skills/command-development/` (7 files: SKILL.md + 6 references)\\n- `../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/skills/plugin-structure/references/component-patterns.md` (Gap 3 decision framework source)\\n\\n**Out of scope for this item (separate backlog):**\\n- `hook-development/`, `mcp-integration/`, `agent-development/`, `plugin-settings/` depth comparison \u2014 identified in rebase analysis as requiring separate full gap analysis. plugin-creator has `hooks-guide` (9 files), `hooks-core-reference`, `hooks-patterns`, `hooks-io-api` skills vs plugin-dev's single `hook-development/` skill with 3 references. Coverage depth is unclear without reading all reference files.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed (if replacing)\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **plugin-creator superset gaps vs anthropic plugin-dev** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Rebase analysis during best-practices.md decomposition (session 2026-03-24)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-24)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nGap identified during superset rebase analysis on 2026-03-24, session `python3-deduplicate` branch.\\n\\n**Observable difference:**\\n\\n1. `../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/skills/command-development/` contains SKILL.md + 6 reference files covering the legacy `commands/` format: frontmatter fields (`disable-model-invocation`, `argument-hint`, `allowed-tools` with Bash filter syntax), argument syntax (`$IF()` conditional, `${1:-default}` defaults), state management via `.local.md` files, workflow locking, rollback patterns, checkpoint/recovery, and a 7-level testing hierarchy. `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/` contains no equivalent skill.\\n\\n2. `plugins/plugin-creator/` has no dedicated `mcp-integration` or `plugin-settings` skill. No `interactive-commands.md` reference file exists in any skill. The hooks-guide covers hooks but does not contain explicit AskUserQuestion/user-interaction patterns documentation.\\n\\n3. `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-plugins-reference-2026/SKILL.md` contains component reference documentation but no explicit \\\"when to use skill vs command vs agent vs hook vs MCP server\\\" decision tree or framework.\\n\\n**How to reproduce gap 1:** Glob `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/` \u2014 returns no files. Glob `../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/skills/command-development/**` \u2014 returns 7 files (SKILL.md + 6 references).\\n\\n**How to reproduce gap 3:** Search `plugins/plugin-creator/` for \\\"when to use\\\", \\\"skill vs agent\\\", \\\"component decision\\\" \u2014 returns 1 partial result (reference documentation, not a decision framework).\\n\\n**Fact-checker note:** The fact-checker marked all 3 claims as REFUTED due to inability to glob the external `claude-plugins-official` directory. This is a tooling failure, not a substantive refutation. The rebase analysis report at `.claude/reports/plugin-dev-rebase-analysis.md` is the verified source and documents gap content in detail. The impact-analyst confirmed the external repo is accessible with 7 files.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n**P1**\\n\\nRationale:\\n\\n1. **Developer tooling completeness** \u2014 plugin-creator is the authoritative guide for plugin development in this repo and marketplace. Every developer building a plugin that includes slash commands has no guidance from plugin-creator. They either guess, use outdated docs, or examine raw plugin-dev source directly. This is a gap in the primary developer-facing tool.\\n\\n2. **Scope of affected use cases** \u2014 the `commands/` format remains a live, supported Claude Code feature. Legacy does not mean removed. Commands with `disable-model-invocation: true` are the correct tool for manual-only workflows. The decision framework gap (Gap 3) affects every plugin author choosing between component types \u2014 not just command users.\\n\\n3. **Asymmetry** \u2014 plugin-creator already positions itself as a superset of plugin-dev (per `plugin-creator extras` section in the rebase report). Gaps undermine that positioning and cause plugin-creator to actively mislead developers (the `commands/` as \\\"legacy format\\\" framing in `claude-code-skills-official.md` implies commands are not worth learning, when in fact `disable-model-invocation` and state-management patterns are not available in skills).\\n\\n4. **Blocking for new skills** \u2014 command-development knowledge (argument syntax, frontmatter fields) is prerequisite content for anyone writing command-based workflows. The absence blocks a complete skill creation workflow.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n**If this gap stays:**\\n\\n1. **Gap 1 (command-development skill)** \u2014 Plugin developers building command-based workflows have no guidance on `disable-model-invocation`, argument syntax (`$IF()`, `${1:-default}`), `.local.md` state management, or workflow locking. They must find this content in plugin-dev directly or guess. Commands created without this knowledge will lack state management, have fragile argument handling, and miss the 7-level testing hierarchy. Quality of command-based plugins in the marketplace degrades.\\n\\n2. **Gap 2 (interactive-commands.md / AskUserQuestion patterns)** \u2014 Commands that need to ask users questions during execution have no documented pattern. Developers either avoid interactive commands entirely (limiting use cases) or implement ad-hoc patterns that diverge from Claude Code conventions.\\n\\n3. **Gap 3 (component decision framework)** \u2014 Plugin developers choose between skills, commands, agents, hooks, and MCP servers without a decision framework. Observable failure mode (documented in Issue Classification): implementing workflows as commands when skills would be cleaner, or as skills when `disable-model-invocation` is the correct tool. Suboptimal component choices increase maintenance cost and reduce plugin quality.\\n\\n**Who is affected:**\\n- All plugin developers using plugin-creator as their primary guide \u2014 including marketplace contributors and internal repo users\\n- Users of resulting plugins \u2014 receive lower-quality plugins built without best-practice patterns\\n\\n**Severity:** The command-development gap is an absolute absence \u2014 there is zero content in plugin-creator about the `commands/` format. The decision framework gap is a documentation depth issue \u2014 component descriptions exist but decision guidance does not. Both affect every plugin author who encounters either use case.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n**Gap 1 \u2014 command-development skill created:**\\n- Developers can build command-based workflows with full knowledge of the `commands/` format: frontmatter fields, argument syntax, state management, and testing hierarchy\\n- Manual-only workflows using `disable-model-invocation: true` become a documented, accessible pattern \u2014 enabling use cases (interactive approval gates, destructive-operation confirmations) that are currently invisible\\n- State-carrying commands using `.local.md` files and workflow locking become reproducible patterns rather than bespoke implementations\\n- plugin-creator reaches true superset status on the command domain\\n\\n**Gap 2 \u2014 interactive-commands reference added:**\\n- AskUserQuestion patterns for commands become discoverable within plugin-creator\\n- Developers writing commands that need user input during execution have a documented pattern to follow\\n- Reduces divergence between plugin-creator-authored commands and Anthropic-standard commands\\n\\n**Gap 3 \u2014 component decision framework added to claude-plugins-reference-2026:**\\n- Plugin developers have a single authoritative answer to \\\"which component should I use?\\\" without reading all component-specific skills first\\n- Reduces component misuse (commands where skills belong, agents where hooks suffice)\\n- Accelerates plugin design: developers reach the right component faster and spend implementation effort on the correct abstraction\\n\\n**Editorial tension resolved (prerequisite benefit):**\\n- The framing in `skill-creator/references/claude-code-skills-official.md` (\\\"commands are legacy\\\") is reconciled with the existence of a command-development skill \u2014 developers receive accurate guidance on when commands are still the right choice vs. when skills are preferred\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter this item is complete, a developer using plugin-creator can:\\n\\n1. **Create a slash command** using `/plugin-creator:command-development` and receive guidance on:\\n   - The `commands/` directory format and when to use commands vs. skills\\n   - All command-specific frontmatter fields: `disable-model-invocation`, `argument-hint`, `allowed-tools` with Bash filter syntax\\n   - Argument handling: positional args, `$ARGUMENTS`, default values, `$IF()` conditional syntax\\n   - State management: persisting state between invocations via `.local.md` files\\n   - Workflow locking to prevent concurrent execution\\n   - Checkpoint/recovery and rollback patterns\\n   - A 7-level testing hierarchy specific to commands\\n\\n2. **Build interactive commands** using AskUserQuestion patterns documented in the command-development skill's interactive-commands reference\\n\\n3. **Decide which component to use** for a given use case by consulting the decision framework in `claude-plugins-reference-2026`, which explicitly addresses: skill vs. command vs. agent vs. hook vs. MCP server \u2014 with criteria and examples\\n\\n4. **Receive accurate framing** on the commands format \u2014 the \\\"legacy\\\" framing is reconciled so it accurately conveys \\\"skills are preferred for new work, AND commands remain the right tool for these specific use cases\\\" rather than implying commands are deprecated\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n**Prerequisites (must complete before authoring Gap 1 content):**\\n- [ ] Editorial decision documented: resolve the \\\"legacy commands\\\" framing tension in `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/claude-code-skills-official.md`. The decision must explicitly state whether commands are deprecated (skills always preferred, no new command skills should be written) or still viable for specific use cases (in which case the new skill co-exists and the existing framing is updated). This decision gates Gap 1 content framing \u2014 do not author the command-development skill before this is resolved.\\n\\n**Gap 1 \u2014 command-development skill:**\\n- [ ] `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/SKILL.md` created \u2014 covers commands vs. skills distinction, command frontmatter fields, argument syntax, and navigation to reference files\\n- [ ] `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/references/frontmatter-reference.md` created \u2014 covers `disable-model-invocation`, `argument-hint` format, `allowed-tools` with Bash filter syntax, documented at reference depth (field type, valid values, when to use, best practices)\\n- [ ] `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/references/advanced-workflows.md` created \u2014 covers `.local.md` state management, workflow locking, checkpoint/recovery, command composition, rollback patterns\\n- [ ] `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/references/interactive-commands.md` created \u2014 covers AskUserQuestion and user-interaction patterns; content sourced from `../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/skills/command-development/references/interactive-commands.md` (verify file is readable before authoring)\\n- [ ] New skill passes `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/`\\n\\n**Gap 3 \u2014 component decision framework:**\\n- [ ] Component decision framework added to `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-plugins-reference-2026/SKILL.md` \u2014 explicitly addresses \\\"when to use skill vs. command vs. agent vs. hook vs. MCP server\\\" with criteria and examples; framed as a decision tree or equivalent navigable structure\\n\\n**Routing updates (consumers):**\\n- [ ] `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-creator/SKILL.md` updated to route \\\"create a command\\\" requests to `plugin-creator:command-development`\\n- [ ] `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md` updated if it orchestrates component creation steps that include commands\\n- [ ] `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-skills-overview-2026/SKILL.md` cross-reference updated to point to new command-development skill (currently notes commands as legacy without pointing to any guidance)\\n\\n**Editorial reconciliation:**\\n- [ ] `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/claude-code-skills-official.md` updated to reflect the editorial decision (either: \\\"commands are fully deprecated \u2014 no new command skills\\\" with pointer removed, or: \\\"commands are viable for X use cases \u2014 see command-development skill\\\")\\n\\n**Gap 2 (scope note):** Gap 2 is covered by the `interactive-commands.md` reference file in Gap 1 above. No separate deliverable.\\n\\n**Gap 4 (out of scope):** hook-development, mcp-integration, agent-development, plugin-settings depth comparison is deferred to a separate backlog item.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n**Source content for Gap 1 and Gap 2:**\\n- `../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/skills/command-development/SKILL.md` \u2014 primary source for command-development skill structure and overview\\n- `../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/skills/command-development/references/frontmatter-reference.md` \u2014 source for command frontmatter field reference\\n- `../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/skills/command-development/references/advanced-workflows.md` \u2014 source for state management, locking, rollback patterns\\n- `../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/skills/command-development/references/interactive-commands.md` \u2014 source for AskUserQuestion patterns (not yet read; verify contents before authoring)\\n- `../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/skills/command-development/references/testing-strategies.md` \u2014 source for 7-level testing hierarchy (Gap 1 content; verify whether to include in plugin-creator scope)\\n- `../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/skills/command-development/references/marketplace-considerations.md` \u2014 review for applicable content; marketplace distribution concerns may be out of scope for plugin-creator audience\\n- `../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/skills/command-development/references/documentation-patterns.md` \u2014 review for applicable content; README patterns for human consumers may be out of scope\\n\\n**Source content for Gap 3:**\\n- `../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/skills/plugin-structure/references/component-patterns.md` \u2014 primary source for component decision framework\\n- `../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/skills/plugin-structure/references/manifest-reference.md` \u2014 may contain structural decision guidance\\n\\n**Rebase analysis (authoritative gap documentation):**\\n- `.claude/reports/plugin-dev-rebase-analysis.md` \u2014 full superset analysis with Already Covered and Gaps sections\\n\\n**Current plugin-creator state:**\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/` \u2014 full plugin directory; read before authoring to avoid duplicating existing content\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/claude-code-skills-official.md` \u2014 contains legacy framing that must be reconciled before authoring Gap 1\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**New files (must be created):**\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/references/frontmatter-reference.md`\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/references/advanced-workflows.md`\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/references/interactive-commands.md`\\n\\n**Modified files:**\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-plugins-reference-2026/SKILL.md` \u2014 add component decision framework (Gap 3)\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-creator/SKILL.md` \u2014 add routing to command-development skill\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/claude-code-skills-official.md` \u2014 resolve legacy-framing editorial tension\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-skills-overview-2026/SKILL.md` \u2014 update commands cross-reference\\n\\n**Modified files (conditional \u2014 verify needed):**\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md` \u2014 update if command creation is part of lifecycle orchestration\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/agent-plugin-ecosystem.md` \u2014 verify command frontmatter portability claims remain accurate once command-development skill is authored\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/audit-skill-completeness/SKILL.md` \u2014 verify whether completeness audit criteria need to include command-development coverage\\n\\n**Auto-updated by pre-commit hook (no manual edit needed):**\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 version bumped automatically on any commit touching plugin-creator files; new skill auto-discovered\\n- `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` \u2014 version bumped automatically\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n**Upstream (this item depends on):**\\n- No blocking upstream items. The source content exists in `../claude-plugins-official/plugins/plugin-dev/` and is accessible. The rebase analysis report is complete.\\n- Internal prerequisite (not a separate backlog item): the editorial decision on legacy-commands framing must be made before Gap 1 content is authored. This is a decision point within this item's execution, not a dependency on another backlog item.\\n\\n**Downstream (should follow this item):**\\n- Gap 4 follow-up backlog item (to be created): full depth comparison of hook-development, mcp-integration, agent-developm